{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond","id":1438336,"title":"How To: Coal to Diamond","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-06T10:31:58-08:00","id":1438336,"title":"How To: Coal to Diamond","content":"Or graphite, fullerenes, or whatever other allotrope. Would Ruling be enough, or would Weaving be required to change an element from one allotrope to another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T11:01:16-08:00","id":1438339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond#post1438336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or graphite, fullerenes, or whatever other allotrope. Would Ruling be enough, or would Weaving be required to change an element from one allotrope to another?</div> </div> </div> </div>Transforming something to something else would be Weaving. It doesn't matter if it's a close substitute. Magic doesn't really care that you're trying to change something to a close representation just that you're trying to change something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T11:32:58-08:00","id":1438341,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Weaving only change stuff like the shape of your coal or, say, the temperature it ignites at, and it requires Patterning to fully transform substance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T11:59:27-08:00","id":1438347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438341#post1438341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Weaving only change stuff like the shape of your coal or, say, the temperature it ignites at, and it requires Patterning to fully transform substance?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct. It is patterning. I just checked my book. I thought it might have been Weaving. This is similar to Space where you can really only teleport at space 4 and there's no real difference between a short teleport and a long one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-06-2021, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T13:11:36-08:00","id":1438348,"title":"","content":"It would require a Patterning Matter spell (aka Matter 4).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Swing on the spiral of our divinity and still be a human&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25961-redzone","name":"Redzone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T18:44:29-08:00","id":1438415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438341#post1438341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Weaving only change stuff like the shape of your coal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ruling is enough to change its shape, say from a hard-edged lump to a panther statuette. MtA2e 156, Shaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T05:45:15-08:00","id":1438459,"title":"","content":"Yeah yeah, that makes the most sense. Ruling can guide the form of what is present, Weaving is for stuff like how large it is, how dense or heavy or effectively burns, Patterning makes one thing into another as Stygia would recognise discrete substances.<br /> <br /> Ruling won't change the molecular structure of carbon from sheets or a lattice into nanotubes, but I think it would be fair game to reshape an existing structure of nanofibre into tubes.<br /> <br /> Hmm, we've got a spell to allow one to visualise atomic and molecular bonds, I think I need to figure out where something like Forces stands on manipulating those energies. I think it should be a bit more than nothing, but not nearly so much as to be kind of broken or completely override Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T22:47:43-08:00","id":1438527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438459#post1438459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, we've got a spell to allow one to visualise atomic and molecular bonds, I think I need to figure out where something like Forces stands on manipulating those energies. I think it should be a bit more than nothing, but not nearly so much as to be kind of broken or completely override Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a bit of a weird one, generally i would say that just avoid any atomics for forces unless explicitly needed, although i imagine the usage of strong forces (as in the binding of atoms, not arcana) or similar things in a mage game is solemn except for a EXTREMLY minute chance if your in a free council focus game and the ST really likes his quantum physics. The supernal simply perceives matter as matter and doesn't perceive the supernal concept of forces in it (except say for example if it is magnetically of electrically charged), its the same way as matter and life, 'technically' life is made of atom like any other object and should be manipulated by matter, but the supernal doesn't care for our semantics. If it says that it ain't matter till its dead, then by god its only becomes matter when its dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26174-blazichaos","name":"Blazichaos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T06:41:30-08:00","id":1438559,"title":"","content":"Reviewing the examples in the main book, I think Weaving is enough to change one allotrope to another, given that it\u2019s enough to turn iron into a room temperature liquid or ice into sub-zero vapour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T07:48:17-08:00","id":1438572,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough I do think changing a material's aggregate state is probably easier than changing allotrope, even though a state changed material would, in fact, be the equivalent of a different allotrope in mundane circumstances (by definition allotropes of an element share the same state, but a state change does very much change the structure of the material). But I don't think it's so difficult that it warrants Patterning. After all, what Weaving can do (alter a subject's properties without outright transforming the subject) should be applicable on things like changing the molecular structure without actually changing any element.<br /> Not to mention how it's probably already possible to switch between allotropes with clever use of other Weaving and Ruling spells by changing other properties until it would form &quot;naturally&quot;. Making it possible with a single spell would just cut out a lot of unnecessary work that would clog up a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-08-2021, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T10:32:02-08:00","id":1438589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438559#post1438559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reviewing the examples in the main book, I think Weaving is enough to change one allotrope to another, given that it\u2019s enough to turn iron into a room temperature liquid or ice into sub-zero vapour.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes down to whether or not one thinks that elements with different molecular configurations count as different substances under Stygian principles. I don't think that's really a matter of technicalities of what they're made of so much as the practical matters of how apparent the differences between them are and how they interact with the world.<br /> <br /> So I think the thing that is going to matter in Stygia is not that graphite and diamond are the same element but how one is soft, black and crumbly and the other is hard, translucent and indestructible. Nanotubes and other novel molecules probably follow the same consideration.<br /> <br /> The fluid iron might not be at melting point temperature, but it probably still has all of the other physical properties of liquid iron, the density and viscosity and such. I think that's a less dramatic distinction than such allotropes have.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do think a Weaving on a sample of graphite could be used to put it into a state where machine-aided physical processes to change the molecular configuration will be much easier, if one has access to such equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T11:00:35-08:00","id":1438594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438589#post1438589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It comes down to whether or not one thinks that elements with different molecular configurations count as different substances under Stygian principles. I don't think that's really a matter of technicalities of what they're made of so much as the practical matters of how apparent the differences between them are and how they interact with the world.<br /> <br /> So I think the thing that is going to matter in Stygia is not that graphite and diamond are the same element but how one is soft, black and crumbly and the other is hard, translucent and indestructible. Nanotubes and other novel molecules probably follow the same consideration.<br /> <br /> The fluid iron might not be at melting point temperature, but it probably still has all of the other physical properties of liquid iron, the density and viscosity and such. I think that's a less dramatic distinction than such allotropes have.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do think a Weaving on a sample of graphite could be used to put it into a state where machine-aided physical processes to change the molecular configuration will be much easier, if one has access to such equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're focusing on the wrong thing. For a Weaving spell it doesn't really matter if the original and the end result are vastly different from each other; only that a Weaving spell can change certain properties. The question is, is the structural makeup of a material considered a property that can be altered by Matter?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fluid iron might not be at melting point temperature, but it probably still has all of the other physical properties of liquid iron, the density and viscosity and such. I think that's a less dramatic distinction than such allotropes have. </div> </div> </div>You do realise that two different allotropes of solid iron would both melt into identical liquid states? Any and all properties shared between one solid allotrope of iron and iron in its liquid form would also be shared by all other solid allotropes of iron. For iron it even happens to be that in the process of melting room temperature iron it will actually cycle through three different allotrope stages (or less, depending on potential additives) before it reaches the melting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T22:14:30-08:00","id":1438685,"title":"","content":"Allotropy is almost always just a fancy phase change so switching between allotropes magically shouldn\u2019t even be a distinct spell from State Change. Changes from one (meta)stable state to another should probably be lasting too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T14:53:38-08:00","id":1438814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438685#post1438685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allotropy is almost always just a fancy phase change so switching between allotropes magically shouldn\u2019t even be a distinct spell from State Change. Changes from one (meta)stable state to another should probably be lasting too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't but even if it were that's not really how magic works. it doesn't matter how close graphite and diamonds are. Turning something into another thing is patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T15:29:09-08:00","id":1438828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438814#post1438814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really isn't but even if it were that's not really how magic works. it doesn't matter how close graphite and diamonds are. Turning something into another thing is patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet turning a solid into a liquid is Weaving. It really depends on what you're affecting. If you transform the entirety of the subject, it's Patterning. If you're transforming a property of the subject (even if that property governs the shape and characteristics of the entire subject, as clearly demonstrated by State Change) it's Weaving.<br /> Is allotropy a property governed by the Matter Arcanum? If yes, then it's absolutely and clearly Weaving. If no, then it's absolutely and clearly Patterning.<br /> Since it is a material property I think the answer is yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T15:35:19-08:00","id":1438829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438814#post1438814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning something into another thing is patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like ice into steam? Because the difference between graphite and diamond is that kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T16:53:53-08:00","id":1438843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438828#post1438828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet turning a solid into a liquid is Weaving. It really depends on what you're affecting. If you transform the entirety of the subject, it's Patterning. If you're transforming a property of the subject (even if that property governs the shape and characteristics of the entire subject, as clearly demonstrated by State Change) it's Weaving.<br /> Is allotropy a property governed by the Matter Arcanum? If yes, then it's absolutely and clearly Weaving. If no, then it's absolutely and clearly Patterning.<br /> Since it is a material property I think the answer is yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it works we're talking about different spells and different associations. solid to liquid is just hitting the melting point on something. Changing something to an allotrope can be any number of factors but more then that it's changing one gross appearance of matter into another. Scientifically and magically those two interactions are different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T16:58:49-08:00","id":1438844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438829#post1438829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like ice into steam? Because the difference between graphite and diamond is that kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not because graphite can't magically turn into a diamond with just heat. Synthetic diamonds are made from pure carbon as are most if not all diamonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T17:26:07-08:00","id":1438849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438844#post1438844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not because graphite can't magically turn into a diamond with just heat. Synthetic diamonds are made from pure carbon as are most if not all diamonds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pressure and heat are the two only factors determining aggregate states (i.e. whether you have solid ice, liquid water, or gaseous vapour) and also the very same factors that determines many (but not all) allotropes. By increasing temperature and reducing pressure you can turn ice into vapour. By increasing temperature and increasing pressure you can turn graphite into diamond. Graphite to diamond is how natural diamonds are formed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T17:51:42-08:00","id":1438853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1438849#post1438849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pressure and heat are the two only factors determining aggregate states (i.e. whether you have solid ice, liquid water, or gaseous vapour) and also the very same factors that determines many (but not all) allotropes. By increasing temperature and reducing pressure you can turn ice into vapour. By increasing temperature and increasing pressure you can turn graphite into diamond. Graphite to diamond is how natural diamonds are formed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not remotely the same and an oversimplification of the amount of work put into it more over the bigger issue is that an allotrope isn't just a simple changed state. Ice into vapor requires no pressure just heat. Magically it's still wouldn't matter if it was possible with just heat. Using matter to change one object to another is forces 4. It doesn't really matter what it is. Ice to water to vapor for the purposes of magic is the same exact thing. They are all water in different forms or iron if you want it's not considered to be something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T20:27:43-08:00","id":1438879,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/courses-images-archive-read-only/wp-content/uploads/sites/53/2014/08/19212109/20140811155434493809.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Carbon-phase-diagramp.svg/1199px-Carbon-phase-diagramp.svg.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T22:57:59-08:00","id":1438892,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you should enlarge on the intended significance of the phase diagrams posted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T12:47:52-08:00","id":1439002,"title":"","content":"Just emphasizing how ice/water vapor and graphite/diamond are in fact fundamentally the same kind of change, and particularly that Epimetheus\u2019s distinction between only \u201cneeding\u201d heat or not is a false one. You can sublimate ice in a vacuum chamber or turn diamond to graphite by heating it enough. How much heat it takes to boil water is known fairly well to depend on altitude. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 03-10-2021, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:12:11-08:00","id":1439029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439002#post1439002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just emphasizing how ice/water vapor and graphite/diamond are in fact fundamentally the same kind of change, and particularly that Epimetheus\u2019s distinction between only \u201cneeding\u201d heat or not is a false one. You can sublimate ice in a vacuum chamber or turn diamond to graphite by heating it enough. How much heat it takes to boil water is known fairly well to depend on altitude. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, have you read the chart. You can't turn graphite into diamond with just heat. You can do that with pressure alone but not heat. However, in my opinion this feels more like a patterning spell then a weaving spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:23:30-08:00","id":1439034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439029#post1439029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, have you read the chart. You can't turn graphite into diamond with just heat. You can do that with pressure alone but not heat. However, in my opinion this feels more like a patterning spell then a weaving spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the axles? Standard atmospheric pressure and normal temperatures is in the &quot;Graphite + Metastable Diamond&quot; field where carbon can exist as both diamonds and graphite. Increase the heat (no change in pressure) and follow the chart directly to the right and you'll find that diamonds no longer have a stable structure and thus becomes graphite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T15:05:16-08:00","id":1439038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439034#post1439034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read the axles? Standard atmospheric pressure and normal temperatures is in the &quot;Graphite + Metastable Diamond&quot; field where carbon can exist as both diamonds and graphite. Increase the heat (no change in pressure) and follow the chart directly to the right and you'll find that diamonds no longer have a stable structure and thus becomes graphite.</div> </div> </div> </div>The units are in giga pascal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T15:06:38-08:00","id":1439039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439029#post1439029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, have you read the chart. You can't turn graphite into diamond with just heat. You can do that with pressure alone but not heat. However, in my opinion this feels more like a patterning spell then a weaving spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter doesn't govern heat, anyway. Liquidity is a property of matter, but liquid steel created via Weaving is the same temperature as the solid steal the Mage used the spell on. Likewise, a crystaline structure is a property of Matter.<br /> <br /> Pressure and heat are both governed by Forces and have nothing to do with the discussion; only that diamond is a state of carbon just like ice and liquid water are states of water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T15:09:27-08:00","id":1439040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439039#post1439039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matter doesn't govern heat, anyway. Liquidity is a property of matter, but liquid steel created via Weaving is the same temperature as the solid steal the Mage used the spell on. Likewise, a crystaline structure is a property of Matter.<br /> <br /> Pressure and heat are both governed by Forces and have nothing to do with the discussion; only that diamond is a state of carbon just like ice and liquid water are states of water.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a reversible state of matter which in my opinion is the most important aspect of it in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T15:27:03-08:00","id":1439043,"title":"","content":"Can I still Weave ice into liquid water in space or do I have to Pattern it? That ice cannot be melted without pressurizing it, heat alone will sublimate it instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T15:33:28-08:00","id":1439045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439043#post1439043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I still Weave ice into liquid water in space or do I have to Pattern it? That ice cannot be melted without pressurizing it, heat alone will sublimate it instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more along the lines of turning graphene into liquid or gas still makes it graphene it doesn't turn it into a diamond. magically graphene is graphene no matter what state it's in. Changing graphene into diamonds is changing one thing into another. It doesn't matter how close they are to each other scientifically. It's not the same material. Whether you change ice to vapor to water back to ice it's still water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-10-2021, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T15:53:48-08:00","id":1439049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439040#post1439040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a reversible state of matter which in my opinion is the most important aspect of it in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it absolutely is reversible. Not under easily achieved circumstances, but that's not a limitation since State Change can absolutely turn tungsten into a gas and even helium into a solid. Helium literally can't exist in a solid state under normal atmospheric pressure.<br /> <br /> Edit: &quot;<a href=\"https://www.desy.de/news/news_search/index_eng.html?openDirectAnchor=1317\" target=\"_blank\">There are different ways to trigger the conversion of diamond to graphite, <b>for instance by simply heating the diamond under exclusion of oxygen</b> or even with an aimed mechanical stroke. The other way round works as well: With heat and high pressure, graphite can be converted into synthetic diamonds that already have quite a market worldwide.</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439045#post1439045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more along the lines of turning graphene into liquid or gas still makes it graphene it doesn't turn it into a diamond. magically graphene is graphene no matter what state it's in. Changing graphene into diamonds is changing one thing into another. It doesn't matter how close they are to each other scientifically. It's not the same material. Whether you change ice to vapor to water back to ice it's still water.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you've made no argument for why different allotropes are considered different materials while different aggregate states are considered the same material. Other than the argument &quot;because it is&quot;, I mean. You're absolutely right in that both ice and vapour is still water. But by the same logic, shouldn't both graphite and diamond both be considered carbon?<br /> Hell, if you do have liquid or gaseous carbon for some contrived reason and cast magic to solidify it, what do you end up with? Liquid carbon is the liquid state of both graphite and diamond because it's the same element. Depending on external forces it could naturally solidify into either allotrope so neither should have any priority over the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-10-2021, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:04:49-08:00","id":1439051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439049#post1439049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you've made no argument for why different allotropes are considered different materials while different aggregate states are considered the same material. Other than the argument &quot;because it is&quot;, I mean. You're absolutely right in that both ice and vapour is still water. But by the same logic, shouldn't both graphite and diamond both be considered carbon?<br /> Hell, if you do have liquid or gaseous carbon for some contrived reason and cast magic to solidify it, what do you end up with? Liquid carbon is the liquid state of both graphite and diamond because it's the same element. Depending on external forces it could naturally solidify into either allotrope so neither should have any priority over the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you can't conceivable turn diamond into graphene despite being a type of elemental carbon it's not the same as graphene. It has different properties. Graphene can't turn into diamond without absurd conditions.<br /> <br /> Magically, since everything is based on platonic concepts. Diamond is diamond. Graphene is graphene. The simplest explanation is that you are trying to turn one item into a different one. Just full stop that's really where it begins and ends. Which means your limited to matter 4. If you wanted to apply magic to making graphene into diamond another way you'd need to use forces. However, I don't think forces let you use that much pressure or heat.<br /> <br /> Also, that's not true. Diamond has more priority over graphene at higher temps and pressures as it's a much more stable form, which is why it can't be turned back into graphene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:14:22-08:00","id":1439053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439051#post1439051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, you can't conceivable turn diamond into graphene despite being a type of elemental carbon it's not the same as graphene. It has different properties. Graphene can't turn into diamond without absurd conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helium can't turn into a solid without absurd conditions. Doesn't stop State Change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439051#post1439051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that's not true. Diamond has more priority over graphene at higher temps and pressures as it's a much more stable form, which is why it can't be turned back into graphene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Graphite, note graphene. Diamond has priority at certain pressures and temperatures, and graphite has priority under under certain pressures and temperatures. Liquid or gaseous carbon isn't part of either range so it solid with a spell leads to a situation where you get solid carbon but no way to determine what properties it should have.<br /> And diamond can be turned into graphite just like graphite can be turned into diamond. I posted a source on that which you probably missed since it was an edit so I'll post it again <a href=\"https://www.desy.de/news/news_search/index_eng.html?openDirectAnchor=1317\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. The thing is, both allotropes are metastable under certain circumstances, meaning once they reach one of those two states they're capable of remaining in that state even if subject to circumstances that would make the other state &quot;more natural&quot; because it would be a lower energy state. But in both cases you can overcompensate the temperature and/or pressure to turn a diamond back into graphite or graphite back into diamond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-10-2021, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:22:58-08:00","id":1439055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439053#post1439053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Graphite, note graphene. Diamond has priority at certain pressures and temperatures, and graphite has priority under under certain pressures and temperatures. Liquid or gaseous carbon isn't part of either range so it solid with a spell leads to a situation where you get solid carbon but no way to determine what properties it should have.<br /> And diamond can be turned into graphite. I posted a source on that which you probably missed since it was an edit so I'll post it again <a href=\"https://www.desy.de/news/news_search/index_eng.html?openDirectAnchor=1317\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant graphite. That's an interesting link, using radiation to get it to switch back. However, magically I'd still say it doesn't really matter. Simply because it's still turning one object into another. It's not altering what's considered a relatively superficial identity which is state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-10-2021, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:38:10-08:00","id":1439059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439055#post1439055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant graphite. That's interesting an interesting link using radiation to get it to switch back.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's <i>one</i> way to do it. In the same article it's also mentioned that <i>heat alone</i> can turn diamond into carbon. (You also need to do it in an oxygen free environment but that's only to avoid igniting the diamond.)<br /> &quot;for instance <b>by simply heating the diamond</b> under exclusion of oxygen&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439055#post1439055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, magically I'd still say it doesn't really matter. Simply because it's still turning one object into another. It's not altering what's considered a relatively superficial identity which is state.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still haven't answered this question: Lets say you raid a lab to steal liquid carbon that's being researched for whatever reason. In order to transport it easier you turn it into a solid. What properties does that solid have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:42:46-08:00","id":1439063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439059#post1439059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's <i>one</i> way to do it. In the same article it's also mentioned that <i>heat alone</i> can turn diamond into carbon. (You also need to do it in an oxygen free environment but that's only to avoid igniting the diamond.)<br /> &quot;for instance <b>by simply heating the diamond</b> under exclusion of oxygen&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I know. I read that I understood that I was speaking incorrectly and just choose to ignore my mistake. It's more that the amount of heat it takes is so high it's normally just implausible to want to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You still haven't answered this question: Lets say you raid a lab to steal liquid carbon that's being researched for whatever reason. In order to transport it easier you turn it into a solid. What properties does that solid have? </div> </div> </div>It'd be a solid block of amorphous carbon. From what I understand after admittedly little reading, liquid carbon has different properties compared to diamond and graphene so magically as a solid it'd have to behave differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-10-2021, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T17:18:07-08:00","id":1439070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439063#post1439063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I know. I read that I understood that I was speaking incorrectly and just choose to ignore my mistake. It's more that the amount of heat it takes is so high it's normally just implausible to want to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet still possible. However, allotropes of other elements can be much, much easier to shift between. For example, iron will pass through multiple different allotropes of its solid state if it's heated from room temperature to its melting point, and melting iron is comparatively simple.<br /> But we also have stuff like helium, which under normal pressure can't be solidified. Literally can't. Despite this I think it's fully possible to change helium into a solid using only Weaving because aggregate states is just a material property and those can be changed with Weaving. The difficulty of doing it mundanely just doesn't factor into Weaving spells (other than possibly for determining Potency or requiring extra Reach, depending on the spell).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It'd be a solid block of amorphous carbon. From what I understand after admittedly little reading, liquid carbon has different properties compared to diamond and graphene so magically as a solid it'd have to behave differently. </div> </div> </div>Well, liquids and solids literally can't share most material properties. This is hardly unique for carbon. The same can be said for iron or even water. Aside from being transparent (and being made from the same elements), there's really nothing that can be said to be common to both liquid water and ice (at least that I can think of right now) because different aggregate states are fundamentally different. Graphite and diamond have much more in common with each other than with liquid carbon just because both are solids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T17:19:14-08:00","id":1439071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439049#post1439049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you've made no argument for why different allotropes are considered different materials while different aggregate states are considered the same material.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Actually when you put it like that it becomes kind of tautological that the two are symbolically different and therefore should at least be different spells. Especially after also considering that State Change as written more intuitively lends itself to liquid diamond (the chemical nonsensicality of that be damned) than to the diamond-graphite transition.<br /> <br /> While that doesn\u2019t settle the Practice question on its own, it does change what substances we should be comparing carbon to to decide. Off the top of my head: glass/quartz (both silicon dioxide), white/red/black phosphorus, anything that exhibits multiple crystal structures. I <i>would</i> single out steel as an especially useful example of the last of those to consider but it would raise the question of \u201cWhat are you magically tempering or detempering steel for that you aren\u2019t better off accomplishing by altering its physical properties directly?\u201d<br /> <br /> ...Which makes me wonder if I might be thinking of the Weaving Practice itself slightly wrong, aaaaaaand in the course of checking on that I\u2019m pretty sure this part of Transubstantiation gives it to Epithemeus:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: The Awakening Second Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The Stygian Mysteries teach that \u201cpurity\u201d is a perceptual concept \u2014 so, for example, even though \u201cwine\u201d and \u201csteel\u201d are made up of numerous compounds, they are concrete enough as concepts to be transmuted).</div> </div> </div> </div><s>Is this what Focused Mage Sight feels like?</s>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T20:51:39-08:00","id":1439092,"title":"","content":"For what it\u2019s worth, if liquid carbon were made solid, I\u2019d expect the end result to be or quickly become graphite, extrapolating from the phase diagram supplied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T00:42:29-08:00","id":1439112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439071#post1439071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Which makes me wonder if I might be thinking of the Weaving Practice itself slightly wrong, aaaaaaand in the course of checking on that I\u2019m pretty sure this part of Transubstantiation gives it to Epithemeus:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (The Stygian Mysteries teach that \u201cpurity\u201d is a perceptual concept \u2014 so, for example, even though \u201cwine\u201d and \u201csteel\u201d are made up of numerous compounds, they are concrete enough as concepts to be transmuted). </div> </div> </div><s>Is this what Focused Mage Sight feels like?</s></div> </div> </div> </div>That quote means that you can treat &quot;wine&quot; and &quot;steel&quot; as a single object, rather than having to target the individual components separately; if you wanted to turn wine into gasoline you could do it with Matter 4 in a single step rather than having to suss out each individual component part and transmute them separately in the right ratios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T04:03:21-08:00","id":1439138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439112#post1439112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That quote means that you can treat &amp;quot;wine&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;steel&amp;quot; as a single object, rather than having to target the individual components separately; if you wanted to turn wine into gasoline you could do it with Matter 4 in a single step rather than having to suss out each individual component part and transmute them separately in the right ratios.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I have to admit, something about phrasing it in this manner and looking back on the wording from Transubstantiation is making me think that it could be valid for Weaving to convert a substance into a perceptually closely related substance. Wine into a different kind of wine, mahogany into oak, one steel alloy into another that doesn't have too many additional components, and maybe even graphite to diamond.<br /> <br /> I'm reassessing the idea of a mage needing to go far to make something like Bucky balls. Not if you're restricted based on how much raw carbon you can acquire, and the spell is still limited to a Duration. How far could it go? I don't think to somewhere crazy.<br /> <br /> Reach could account for something more exotic under this principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T04:19:54-08:00","id":1439142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439112#post1439112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That quote means that you can treat &amp;quot;wine&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;steel&amp;quot; as a single object, rather than having to target the individual components separately; if you wanted to turn wine into gasoline you could do it with Matter 4 in a single step rather than having to suss out each individual component part and transmute them separately in the right ratios.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's a difference between a pure element and a complex compound. Magic doesn't opperate the same way science does in the game. There are times when you can't do something at lower dots and have to wait until you have more knowledge about it. Just because alletropes exist in real life doesn't mean magic has any way to treat them as an exception. For the purposes of magic, objects are one concrete thing and changing them into another requires patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T04:50:48-08:00","id":1439147,"title":"","content":"Patterning is required for total transformations and Weaving is used for transforming specific aspects of a subject. I think we can all agree on that.<br /> For Matter, these specific aspects are often various material properties, which is why Alter Conductivity is a Matter spell and not a Forces spell (an equivalent Forces spell would instead simply ignore conductivity). Aggregate states are also material properties, meaning that despite water and ice being highly unlike each other and the shift between them very much looking like a complete transformation, it's still a matter (heh) of Weaving rather than Patterning. I think we can agree on this as well.<br /> Well, allotropy is also a material property. You're just used to thinking about graphite and diamond as different substances, but they are the very same element and goes through phase transitions to each other based on pressure and temperature, just like aggregate states. Diamond happens to be metastable, but aggregate states can also be metastable. Supercooled water remains liquid below its freezing point until external force brings it out of balance and it freezes. Allotropes and aggregate states are basically the same thing.<br /> The thing is, you're just used to thinking about the different aggregate states of water as the same material, and the different allotropes of carbon as separate materials, but anyone who recognises that allotropy (much like aggregate states, and less dramatic) is a material property should be able to change that property with a Weaving spell. <i>Not</i> allowing that would be the exception.<br /> Alternatively you can look to the dramatic differences between some allotropes and consider them different materials, but then considering different aggregate states as being the same material would be the exception because then ice should be a concrete material that requires Patterning to transform into liquid water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-11-2021, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T05:30:31-08:00","id":1439152,"title":"","content":"For me, it's more about the overall transformation. You aren't altering a function of what diamond can do. You are transforming that diamond. That it has the same chemical make up as graphite doesn't matter. If you were to use alter state on diamonds or graphite to liquid or gas it would go back to what it orginally was if you turned it into a solid again. I understand that scientifically they both have the same elemental composition with a different molecular structure. However, magically that's not the case. These are two different conceptual items and you are trying to alter one to be the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:05:11-08:00","id":1439158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439152#post1439152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, it's more about the overall transformation. You aren't altering a function of what diamond can do. You are transforming that diamond. If you were to use alter state on diamonds or graphite to liquid or gas</div> </div> </div> </div>How in any world does changing a solid into a liquid not alter the function of what that solid can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:58:29-08:00","id":1439170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439158#post1439158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How in any world does changing a solid into a liquid not alter the function of what that solid can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mispoke. It's not that it doesn't alter the function just that it doesn't alter the innate being of it. If you changed graphite into liquid carbon and applied the necessary heat and pressue to it, it could become a diamond. However, if you used magic to mess with it and then turned it back into a solid, it would just turn back into graphene. Magic just uses different rules then science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:09:54-08:00","id":1439174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439158#post1439158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How in any world does changing a solid into a liquid not alter the function of what that solid can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because conservation of energy does not apply to that transformation. If you liquefy a rock, you will have a room temperature liquid rock rather than magma. You can create ice gas, an oxygen sword or skates made out of solid water (rather than ice). The mage's Gnosis simply says &quot;You are in this state of matter now, this is your new reality. Rules of physics, go cry in a corner until I release this Imago&quot;. The trick is that any properties that are tangential to the main effect are not affected, such as elasticity or electrical conductivity. Which means traditional physics will not help you make sense of how the effect happened, but allow you to come up with clever applications for its consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T16:44:49-08:00","id":1439540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439147#post1439147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allotropes and aggregate states are basically the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you\u2019ve made the statement too strong. While they\u2019re both kinds of physical phases, one involves a possibly drastic change in molecular structure and the other doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, you're just used to thinking about the different aggregate states of water as the same material, and the different allotropes of carbon as separate materials </div> </div> </div>\u201cPurity is a perceptual concept\u201d implies that this is as above, so below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T17:28:00-08:00","id":1439552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439540#post1439540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cPurity is a perceptual concept\u201d implies that this is as above, so below.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I expect many in the Free Council would argue it's the other way around, that this particular principle arises from the flawed perception of humanity across most of history, and that even most modern people who might intellectually recognise that graphite and diamond are the same substance or that there's no such thing as pure wine don't really feel it intuitively.<br /> <br /> I can imagine some Libertine, or even a significant group of them up to the level of a Legacy, have an Obsession with trying to change this perception on a fundamental enough level that Matter spells actually would operate more in line with the understanding of modern chemistry. I would see such mages thinking that the discrepancy would be a very readily demonstrated aspect of their belief system and that to actually alter things to the point where the Supernal laws demonstrate it would be a major coup for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T22:58:37-08:00","id":1439599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439540#post1439540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you\u2019ve made the statement too strong. While they\u2019re both kinds of physical phases, one involves a possibly drastic change in molecular structure and the other doesn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean molecular arrangement, and I consider the difference between amorphous and three dimensional crystalline considerably less drastic than solid and fluid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T06:32:02-08:00","id":1439637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439540#post1439540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you\u2019ve made the statement too strong. While they\u2019re both kinds of physical phases, one involves a possibly drastic change in molecular structure and the other doesn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Most allotropes are not nearly as drastically different as opposed to different aggregate states.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cPurity is a perceptual concept\u201d implies that this is as above, so below. </div> </div> </div>To me it implies it's a subjective matter. If it was a matter of consensus, we'd end up with State Change not being able to solidify lava/magma as those two substances are dramatically different in the minds of people. Rather, I believe it's fully reasonable to use Patterning to transform graphite to diamond from the perspective of those being different materials, but equally viable to use Weaving to change the material property of allotropy of graphite, which also results in diamond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T09:00:51-08:00","id":1439673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439637#post1439637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it implies it's a subjective matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not how anything else works in Mage: the Awakening, and runs counter to the premise that this is based on power over essential forms.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that statement is in there precisely to establish a ruling on how this kind of magic works specifically to avoid arguments such as this, over whether Matter can be made to run on modern chemistry, or differently depending on somebody's level of education.<br /> <br /> The kind of thing I only ever know of writer statements that it's not really intended to work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:35:28-08:00","id":1439748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1439599#post1439599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you mean molecular arrangement, and I consider the difference between amorphous and three dimensional crystalline considerably less drastic than solid and fluid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean how water is still<br /> <img src=\"https://media.sciencephoto.com/image/a7000381/800wm\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> in every phase whereas carbon goes<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/BNAZO1FplaQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T14:34:06-07:00","id":1440498,"title":"","content":"Uhh that's... not correct.<br /> <br /> Water in ice forms regular crystal structures held together by various forces, such as hydrogen bonds.So water in ice is this:<br /> <img src=\"https://qph.fs.quoracdn.net/main-qimg-d67721a8c474b0ced586f643bd97cae9.webp\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Meanwhile in liquid water there is no regular structure but the molecules are still bound together to a degree, that single molecule of water you posted could only represent a state of water in it's gaseous form. A change of state is a much bigger change than change of allotropy.<br /> <br /> Additionaly while graphite doesn't change into diamonds on it's own, the reverse process is actually thermodynamically favored. It's just excruciatingly slow (talking bilions of years) but hey with Time you can do it!. How it does affect this discussion I dunno, guess you could allow for it go one way but not the other but that's a bit too nitpicky for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 03-18-2021, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T16:17:00-07:00","id":1440505,"title":"","content":"Ok, so while everything about the subject seems to have been more or less said, but here is something to throw out there- did you know that there are a number of phases for ice? Like, some phases of ice can only form under great pressure, and the properties of the different phases are different from one another, so even saying &quot;I transform water into ice&quot; is not trivial. Would anyone here have a problem with the same Practice which allows you to turn water into different phases of ice, or even turn ice from one phase to another? If not, the same holds true for coal and diamonds In the end, what we call &quot;states of matter&quot; (which are simply approximations which are generally good to day to day life) simply measure how well defined is the structure of the material- or how much entropy it had. Diamonds are one such structure, which is very unfavorable because you may say that its crustal structure is too &quot;perfect&quot; (it is very close to a perfect crystal, which entropy really doesn't like). The other, more common crystal structures are simply more stable because they have a greater entropy. Now, while Mage clearly doesn't care about physics, if you decide that a certain Practice is enough to change water into ice, and &quot;all that it does&quot; is changing the arrangement of particles, the change is much less fundamental than, say change water and CO2 into sugar, or worse, change carbon into iron. Diamond and graphene are not the same material, but they are built using the same units, and as such a transformation of coal to diamonds may be more difficult than changing water into ice, but it is definitely the same process.<br /> <br /> So yeah, while you don't need two degrees in chemistry, do your M.Sc and PhD projects in a solid state laboratory and dedicate your life to investigating the contribution of entropy to the stability of materials, it does help to say &quot;yeah, that's basically the same thing- like, it is waaaaaaaay more difficult because, like, ENTROPY, but you don't give a damn about the conservation of energy anyway so... yeah, magic&quot;<br /> <br /> (God what happened to my life...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T19:45:11-07:00","id":1440532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440498#post1440498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhh that's... not correct.<br /> <br /> Water in ice forms regular crystal structures held together by various forces, such as hydrogen bonds.So water in ice is this:<br /> <img src=\"https://qph.fs.quoracdn.net/main-qimg-d67721a8c474b0ced586f643bd97cae9.webp\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Meanwhile in liquid water there is no regular structure but the molecules are still bound together to a degree, that single molecule of water you posted could only represent a state of water in it's gaseous form. A change of state is a much bigger change than change of allotropy.<br /> <br /> Additionaly while graphite doesn't change into diamonds on it's own, the reverse process is actually thermodynamically favored. It's just excruciatingly slow (talking bilions of years) but hey with Time you can do it!. How it does affect this discussion I dunno, guess you could allow for it go one way but not the other but that's a bit too nitpicky for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time doesn't let you go billions of years into the future. Neither does Forces actually let you put in the Work needed to create diamonds from those abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-18T21:47:43-07:00","id":1440543,"title":"","content":"I think it's fair to say that the point at which people are pulling out complex diagrams to justify how their roleplaying game is arbitrated, they're departing quite far from the intended application of the rules and story.<br /> <br /> Awakening at least has a coherent internal logic for why a Masters in Chemistry does not allow one to find shortcuts around the Practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T09:13:01-07:00","id":1440608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440543#post1440543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakening at least has a coherent internal logic for why a Masters in Chemistry does not allow one to find shortcuts around the Practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the opposite, Awakening has coherent internal logic for why a Masters in Chemistry <i>does</i> allow one to find shortcuts around the Practices, because exploiting Fallen Laws is definitely a thing Mages do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's fair to say that the point at which people are pulling out complex diagrams to justify how their roleplaying game is arbitrated, they're departing quite far from the intended application of the rules and story. </div> </div> </div><br /> I also find the &quot;well, you're pulling out science charts so you're wrong, 'cause magic&quot; to be the most bad faith argument that can be advanced; just because a particular individual believes that their particular semiotic view should reign supreme over actual demonstrable fact (and anyone else's semiotic view) doesn't mean they are correct or can't be challenged with evidence (even scientific evidence in a magic game) that their semiotic view is <i>wrong</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T10:30:32-07:00","id":1440614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440532#post1440532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time doesn't let you go billions of years into the future. Neither does Forces actually let you put in the Work needed to create diamonds from those abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually does, all you need is Temporal Stutter with indefinite duration and a conditional duration for the target exit point. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could add Mind 1 to allow yourself to exist in both times and dynamically alter the past/present to create the optimal future. While technically your future self is existing in a theoretical timeline and making decisions based on the highest probable outcome estimated by a Prophecy like simulation, it can still be a powerful tool. Time travel is a lot easier to accomplish working forwards rather than backwards, but a lot more difficult to manage when traveling billions of years due to the massive culture drift of a new epoch, which is only exacerbated by the high information volume of a globalized civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T12:40:43-07:00","id":1440621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440614#post1440614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually does, all you need is Temporal Stutter with indefinite duration and a conditional duration for the target exit point. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could add Mind 1 to allow yourself to exist in both times and dynamically alter the past/present to create the optimal future. While technically your future self is existing in a theoretical timeline and making decisions based on the highest probable outcome estimated by a Prophecy like simulation, it can still be a powerful tool. Time travel is a lot easier to accomplish working forwards rather than backwards, but a lot more difficult to manage when traveling billions of years due to the massive culture drift of a new epoch, which is only exacerbated by the high information volume of a globalized civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked, temporal stutter still has limits that don't let you exceed it even with an infinite duration. Also, that assumes humanity or even earth still exists in a billion years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T14:35:27-07:00","id":1440637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440608#post1440608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would argue the opposite, Awakening has coherent internal logic for why a Masters in Chemistry <i>does</i> allow one to find shortcuts around the Practices, because exploiting Fallen Laws is definitely a thing Mages do.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are your other examples of that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also find the &quot;well, you're pulling out science charts so you're wrong, 'cause magic&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about magic, and it's not even about being wrong. It's about the idea that it's a level of elaboration that severely departs from what is straightforwardly functional for playing a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">just because a particular individual believes that their particular semiotic view should reign supreme over actual demonstrable fact (and anyone else's semiotic view) doesn't mean they are correct or can't be challenged with evidence (even scientific evidence in a magic game) that their semiotic view is <i>wrong</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a perspective that a person is free to bring to critique of the game, but it really is at odds with how the game itself presents things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time I checked, temporal stutter still has limits that don't let you exceed it even with indefinite duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how it does. &quot;The subject completely vanishes from the Fallen World, and reappears unchanged when the spell's Duration ends.&quot; You might be thinking about how a subject within a Temporal Pocket still experiences a personal passage of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T14:54:34-07:00","id":1440641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440637#post1440637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are your other examples of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are numerous examples in the book: <i>Control Light</i> lets you turn a lamp into a laser (requires you to know what a laser is, not happening in Dark Eras); having dots in Crafts makes <i>Shaping</i> more effective; <i>Control Gravity</i> can have all sorts of fun secondary effects with a bit of calculus and physics; and the more you know about biology and what's possible for a body to accomplish the more different traits you can come up with for <i>Transform Life</i>; and that's just a few examples off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not about magic, and it's not even about being wrong. It's about the idea that it's a level of elaboration that severely departs from what is straightforwardly functional for playing a game. </div> </div> </div>Then it's on the other party not to start the argument in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a perspective that a person is free to bring to critique of the game, but it really is at odds with how the game itself presents things. </div> </div> </div>That does not make sense in the context of what I wrote unless you're advocating the idea that the first person to push a semiotic view gets to be &quot;right&quot; despite any evidence to the contrary because that's how the game sets things up.<br /> <br /> Which... I'm going to assume that's not your actual view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 03-19-2021, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T15:10:17-07:00","id":1440646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440641#post1440641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are numerous examples in the book: <i>Control Light</i> lets you turn a lamp into a laser (requires you to know what a laser is, not happening in Dark Eras); having dots in Crafts makes <i>Shaping</i> more effective; <i>Control Gravity</i> can have all sorts of fun secondary effects with a bit of calculus and physics; and the more you know about biology and what's possible for a body to accomplish the more different traits you can come up with for <i>Transform Life</i>; and that's just a few examples off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read Dark Eras but there are no mechanical differences from having those skills and not having them when it comes to spells. They don't specifically apply any additional benefit to spells that can't be used in other ways. That is, yes you can flavor your spell rotes with math and physics using the academics skill but that's no different then someone else using another skill. Those abilities don't apply to magic any more potently then any other method because magic at the end of the day is overwriting the laws of physics to impose your will on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T15:12:06-07:00","id":1440647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440637#post1440637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it does. &quot;The subject completely vanishes from the Fallen World, and reappears unchanged when the spell's Duration ends.&quot; You might be thinking about how a subject within a Temporal Pocket still experiences a personal passage of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of the 1e version which still only limits it to at most a couple hundred years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T15:26:13-07:00","id":1440648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440646#post1440646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't read Dark Eras but there are no mechanical differences from having those skills and not having them when it comes to spells. They don't specifically apply any additional benefit to spells that can't be used in other ways. That is, yes you can flavor your spell rotes with math and physics using the academics skill but that's no different then someone else using another skill. Those abilities don't apply to magic any more potently then any other method because magic at the end of the day is overwriting the laws of physics to impose your will on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about rote skills.<br /> <br /> If calculus hasn't been invented yet, you're not able to calculate things like deflection due to the Coriolis effect, if geometry hasn't been invented yet you can't calculate arc trajectories at all (and you're not going to be able to just guess over long distances without lots of experience). If you've never seen the Taj Mahal you're not going to be able to use <i>Shaping</i> to create a replica out of ice. If no one knows that light can be collimated, then it doesn't matter how much magic you have, you're not collimating light.<br /> <br /> You are also confusing <i>primary effects</i> (which are the spell itself) with <i>secondary effects</i> (things caused by the spell but not part of the spell).<br /> <br /> Also, you are literally wrong when it comes to <i>Shaping</i>, it explicitly states that intricate shapes might require a Wits + Crafts roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T15:42:09-07:00","id":1440651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440648#post1440648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not talking about rote skills.<br /> <br /> If calculus hasn't been invented yet, you're not able to calculate things like deflection due to the Coriolis effect, if geometry hasn't been invented yet you can't calculate arc trajectories at all (and you're not going to be able to just guess over long distances without lots of experience). If you've never seen the Taj Mahal you're not going to be able to use <i>Shaping</i> to create a replica out of ice. If no one knows that light can be collimated, then it doesn't matter how much magic you have, you're not collimating light.<br /> <br /> You are also confusing <i>primary effects</i> (which are the spell itself) with <i>secondary effects</i> (things caused by the spell but not part of the spell).<br /> <br /> Also, you are literally wrong when it comes to <i>Shaping</i>, it explicitly states that intricate shapes might require a Wits + Crafts roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, it doesn't matter. You're using magic. You don't need to do those things. Moreover, no one can do those things in their head except 0.001% of the population. The rest use a program like mathematica or if they want to spend days on one calculation, a paper and calculator. Under those rules no one could ever do that using magic. However, nothing I've seen prevents any mage -no matter how stupid- from turning anything into a laser. That's not supported by the rules.<br /> <br /> Second off, shaping's ruling says it says might. Lastly, crafts have nothing to do with science which is where calculous and geometry go and wits isn't intelligence. Currently, a skilled woodworker can do it just as well as an engineer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 03-19-2021, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T17:54:23-07:00","id":1440664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440641#post1440641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are numerous examples in the book: <i>Control Light</i> lets you turn a lamp into a laser (requires you to know what a laser is, not happening in Dark Eras)</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't require you to have any idea of how lasers work, you just need to be able to know what they are.<br /> <br /> The idea that changes in the surrounding cultural context expands the range of what mages can conceptualise is all well and good, but that's a distinct thing from harnessing something like atomic theory to find ways of altering matter that are not governed by the parameters of the Practices or the explicit statement that material purity is a perceptual phenomenon for the purposes of spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Control Gravity</i> can have all sorts of fun secondary effects with a bit of calculus and physics</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not even in the book, that's an assertion of your own.<br /> <br /> The idea that a person can be creative with how they angle a person's altered vectors would be a distinct thing from &quot;mages can actively exploit-<br /> <br /> Okay, now I can see how your statement of &quot;this is definitely a thing they do&quot; is based entirely in your own supposition, rather than being something you're asserting that the books state.<br /> <br /> I find it an odd way to say something that practically comes down to &quot;a mage who conjures fire knows they can make that spread on its own if they throw it at something flammable&quot;, and that still doesn't have anything to do with the idea that in-depth knowledge of material science changes the dots needed to change one material into a significantly different one.<br /> <br /> Looking back on it, I think the arguments surrounding the capacity of Weaving to make states of matter with impossible temperatures were missing the idea that such a thing is a clear demonstration that the intervention of magic interacts with substances in ways far removed from how they operate or differentiate mundanely.<br /> <br /> As for the cases that go back to things such as this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the more you know about biology and what's possible for a body to accomplish the more different traits you can come up with for <i>Transform Life</i>; and that's just a few examples off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might come back more to something where what a mage can visualise serves as an inspiration for what their Art contrives.<br /> <br /> But really, adding a trait that they know to exist to an animal doesn't say that they're harnessing Fallen Laws, it means that those animal traits effectively function in the Supernal.<br /> <br /> The Supernal gets privileges from the fact that you can graft a functioning venom sack into a Pattern that probably doesn't otherwise have the chains of biochemistry that actually synthesize venom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does not make sense in the context of what I wrote unless you're advocating the idea that the first person to push a semiotic view gets to be &quot;right&quot; despite any evidence to the contrary because that's how the game sets things up.<br /> <br /> Which... I'm going to assume that's not your actual view.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's not my view of reality, if that's what you're saying.<br /> <br /> In the context of the fiction of Mage: the Awakening, the manner in which they cast spells isn't really about a view that somebody pushed at one point, it's that Awakened people made reasoned observations about how their magic worked. That in the Supernal, and through the lens of their Gnosis, willworkers are aware of principles of reality that transcend and supersede how they function without the intervention of magic.<br /> <br /> That a person can be made to fly without regard for aerodynamics is not supposed to be a thing that arises from ignorance, and then once discoveries about how objects travel at speed through air it becomes necessary to cast spells whose effects account for those details. <br /> <br /> In Mage: the Awakening Second Edition, semiotics is a matter of what allows a mage to have shorthand for imagining subjects in terms of their essential forms. The sun at noon as an aid to forming the Imago that sees through falsehoods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T19:29:41-07:00","id":1440675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440621#post1440621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last time I checked, temporal stutter still has limits that don't let you exceed it even with an infinite duration. Also, that assumes humanity or even earth still exists in a billion years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just checked in page 189 of the core book. There are no apparent limits for Temporal Stutter short of it being dispelled, which is true for all spells. In addition, the clause set by conditional duration does not need to be reliant on humanity, you can simply set a given amount of time. This does not guarantee that humanity is still present, on the planet or that the planet hasn't been destroyed, moved or unrecognizably terraformed by that time. But that only means that, similar to all great workings involving Time magic, careful and methodical preparation is key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-19-2021, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T19:48:37-07:00","id":1440678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440675#post1440675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, the clause set by conditional duration does not need to be reliant on humanity, you can simply set a given amount of time. This does not guarantee that humanity is still present, on the planet or that the planet hasn't been destroyed, moved or unrecognizably terraformed by that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is talking about the fact that you literally gave more attention to the prospect of culture drift than the continued survival of humanity in your talk about &quot;time travel [being] easier to accomplish working forwards rather than backwards.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a setting where, without getting into vampires and mummy cults and Deviant conspiracies and the swelling ranks of ghostly Reapers, <i>the Seers and the Scelesti exist</i>.<br /> <br /> If I'm worried about societal drift on a timescale you could measure a geological age with, it's in an Emanation Realm or an Annunaki, not the Phenomenal World as it's interacted with by the Awakened, whose shelf life is looking increasingly short with or without catastrophic apocalyptic events coming into play within the next century or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-19T20:34:52-07:00","id":1440681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440675#post1440675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I just checked in page 189 of the core book. There are no apparent limits for Temporal Stutter short of it being dispelled, which is true for all spells. In addition, the clause set by conditional duration does not need to be reliant on humanity, you can simply set a given amount of time. This does not guarantee that humanity is still present, on the planet or that the planet hasn't been destroyed, moved or unrecognizably terraformed by that time. But that only means that, similar to all great workings involving Time magic, careful and methodical preparation is key.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was with that second comment that the earth could be a lifeless, sterile rock, that'll kill you in seconds after you arrive or worse maybe the sun is in the process of being a red dwarf due to miscalculations made a billion years ago and it's already engulfed the earth. So you're going to arrive at instant death. Just seems like an insanely stupid idea in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T03:46:20-07:00","id":1440703,"title":"","content":"Hmm, there are a few Shielding spells that could probably keep you alive for their Duration. Even within the scope of Time, use that spell that prevents any changes from occurring to the subject.<br /> <br /> It takes an Adept to send somebody to the future, but if a Master provides them with the spell to then return to the moment before they vanished and call it off, they wouldn't need to leave and could report on what they'd seen.<br /> <br /> Hmm, if I understand the spell correctly, a person who did that would still return to the point in the distant future. It's just that now they've created a past where they stuck around while also producing an account of the future.<br /> <br /> In gameplay terms, probably more a thing to hear about than to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T07:00:21-07:00","id":1440711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440681#post1440681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was with that second comment that the earth could be a lifeless, sterile rock, that'll kill you in seconds after you arrive or worse maybe the sun is in the process of being a red dwarf due to miscalculations made a billion years ago and it's already engulfed the earth. So you're going to arrive at instant death. Just seems like an insanely stupid idea in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was focusing on the viability of the spell, since it is technically doable. The necessity of doing it is probably low, but I imagine there is a situation for it, provided proper planning is done to guarantee safe arrival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-20T07:32:33-07:00","id":1440714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1440703#post1440703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, there are a few Shielding spells that could probably keep you alive for their Duration. Even within the scope of Time, use that spell that prevents any changes from occurring to the subject.<br /> <br /> It takes an Adept to send somebody to the future, but if a Master provides them with the spell to then return to the moment before they vanished and call it off, they wouldn't need to leave and could report on what they'd seen.<br /> <br /> Hmm, if I understand the spell correctly, a person who did that would still return to the point in the distant future. It's just that now they've created a past where they stuck around while also producing an account of the future.<br /> <br /> In gameplay terms, probably more a thing to hear about than to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might work, especially since Veil of Moments fills that Shielding requirement nicely, although I had something different in mind. In the present there are a near infinite amount of possible paths, you choose one of those branches and that becomes your new present. This spell makes it so you instead choose [Potency] and then collapse their results into the present timeline. If you ever programmed using version control, its similar to that.<br /> <br /> When making the time clone, one approach is to shuffle your conciousness between possibilities, which means only one can act unless you use Mind 1. Alternatively, each of them can act independently and you keep tabs of them via a Mind 2 telepathic link.<br /> <br /> Drawing a parallel to D&amp;D, you create an Echo Knight style clone with some monitoring extras and then apply Temporal Stutter upon it. There is more to this spell thought, I have been thinking about it for a while and might codify it in Creative Thaumaturgy soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-20-2021, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T14:04:26-07:00","id":1458253,"title":"","content":"Sorry for Necroing, but I think there's a pretty straight forward answer I haven't seen anyone mention among all the chemistry and the graphs and maybe someone will find it useful: <b>This is literally the effect of Crucible (Perfecting) </b>The Potency determines the quality of the Diamond/s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","user":"EW-Matias","date":". 09-01-2021, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T14:44:45-07:00","id":1458257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458253#post1458253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for Necroing, but I think there's a pretty straight forward answer I haven't seen anyone mention among all the chemistry and the graphs and maybe someone will find it useful: <b>This is literally the effect of Crucible (Perfecting) </b>The Potency determines the quality of the Diamond/s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing a diamond's value/purity/quality does not change its allotrope. And even if it did, it would only be a side effect of the actual effect (which is increased quality regardless of its chemical structure) and not necessarily be applicable on other materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T14:47:26-07:00","id":1458259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458253#post1458253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>This is literally the effect of Crucible (Perfecting) </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Not it isn't. Crucible causes already valuable material to become more valuable; it's phrased in terms of altering composition in subtle ways that enhance how they would be valued, but I think it could even be regarded in terms of just lending some extra nebulous quality that attracts people. In any case, it doesn't turn something else into diamond.<br /> <br /> Cast Crucible on a piece of coal and I expect that you'll just get coal that burns very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T22:08:14-07:00","id":1458301,"title":"","content":"I think that any physical object that has an Availability rating should be able to be improved by Cruible, and anything that is a commodity should have an Availability rating of at least 1. After all, coal doesn't grow on wild trees. You need *some* disposable income to get some trivially, and other methods you can come up for getting &quot;free&quot; coal require at least some effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","user":"EW-Matias","date":". 09-02-2021, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T22:17:04-07:00","id":1458303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458257#post1458257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Increasing a diamond's value/purity/quality does not change its allotrope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says that? Diamonds and coal are the sane substance, dianonds are what we call the more besutiful abd useful for tool making form of coal. That's exactly what crucible is for.<br /> <br /> As someone said before,you could change every single characteristic of the coal to make it like those of a diamond one by one by perfecting and weaving and no one could argue with that, so having a spell that does it all at once for ease of play seems hard to argue against, and indeed there is one that already fits the bill in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","user":"EW-Matias","date":". 09-02-2021, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T00:56:21-07:00","id":1458309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458303#post1458303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says that? Diamonds and coal are the sane substance, dianonds are what we call the more besutiful abd useful for tool making form of coal. That's exactly what crucible is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not the same substance (as evident by this very thread). One of the examples is making a diamond more valuable; which I believe is quite telling for how the spell is intended to work.<br /> I would argue that some materials might change allotrope through use of this spell (such as metals gaining more valuable characteristics) but, again, that would be a side effect of the spell that wouldn't be applicable on all substances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As someone said before,you could change every single characteristic of the coal to make it like those of a diamond one by one by perfecting and weaving and no one could argue with that, so having a spell that does it all at once for ease of play seems hard to argue against, and indeed there is one that already fits the bill in the core book. </div> </div> </div>I was the one who said that (not exactly; but something to the same effect), and I'm one of those who argued that changing the allotrope of a substance should be possible through a single spell. But Crucible is just not that spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T05:07:34-07:00","id":1458319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458303#post1458303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diamonds and coal are the sane substance</div> </div> </div> </div>Coal and diamond are the same substance to about the same degree as diamond and human flesh are.<br /> <br /> Like, the mass of coal is technically primarily carbon, but it's carbon bundled up with a lot of hydrogen and some other elements, and depending on composition there might be other organic compounds mixed in there as well. The Transubstantiation spell establishes that in Supernal terms, the purity of a substance is largely a perceptual thing, so something that is technically a mixture such as wine will have many spells that treat it as a contiguous thing as much as they would pure mercury.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">dianonds are what we call the more besutiful abd useful for tool making form of coal</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Nobody who actually knows anything about material science calls diamonds that. I think most people who get their ideas of the relationship between the two from Superman comics wouldn't actually make that leap.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T09:44:06-07:00","id":1458369,"title":"","content":"What you mean is that turning coal to a diammond requires eliminating impuruties and improving it's molecular structure... seems exactly what Crucible does.<br /> <br /> I honestly can't comprehend this debate coming ftom anywhere else than pedantry. Is coal carbon?Is a diamond Carbon? Is the Diamond more vauable? That's all that matters<br /> <br /> Would you object to me using a random piece of scrap steel and perfecting it into a very specific forn of steel I need for a specific use, even if it involves changing it's compsition and sructure? I doubt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T10:46:59-07:00","id":1458381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458369#post1458369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you mean is that turning coal to a diammond requires eliminating impuruties</div> </div> </div> </div>Is water impure oxygen?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">improving it's molecular structure</div> </div> </div> </div>Molecular structure is not a concept recognised in the Supernal. How spells interact with what a thing is and what its qualities are is more metaphysical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is coal carbon?Is a diamond Carbon? Is the Diamond more vauable? That's all that matters</div> </div> </div> </div>No, what matters is whether there are Supernal symbols for fine molecular composition or whether they deal with things in terms of how they're generally perceived and interacted with. The presentation of the game leans towards the latter.<br /> <br /> That and your interpretation goes for a weird thing where all organic chemicals are treated interchangeably. I already mentioned flesh, but what about, say, methane; do you think that makes sense as something to perfect into diamond?<br /> <br /> Mind, that raises questions about what metric of value is actually being applied. Perfecting precious minerals on grounds of making them more valuable versions of themselves is all well and good, but when used as a basis for turning one substance into a completely different one it makes people need to rule on whether there's more value in fuel than looking pretty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you object to me using a random piece of scrap steel and perfecting it into a very specific forn of steel I need for a specific use, even if it involves changing it's compsition and sructure? I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something very important in how both ends of your equation there contain the word steel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 09-02-2021, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T11:13:39-07:00","id":1458383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458381#post1458381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is water impure oxygen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Coal and diamond are both 100% carbon, water is not only composed of Oxygen.<br /> <br /> That said: I also don't think <i>Crucible</i> is the spell for this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Molecular structure is not a concept recognised in the Supernal. </div> </div> </div>[citation needed]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How spells interact with what a thing is and what it's qualities are is more metaphysical. </div> </div> </div>It <i>can be</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, what matters is whether there are Supernal symbols for fine molecular composition or whether they deal with things in terms of how they're generally perceived and interacted with. The presentation of the game leans towards the latter.<br /> <br /> That and your interpretation goes for a weird thing where all organic chemicals are treated interchangeably. I already mentioned flesh, but what about, say, methane; do you think that makes sense as something to perfect into diamond? </div> </div> </div>Methane is not an allotrope of carbon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T11:32:57-07:00","id":1458389,"title":"","content":"If you wanna have a completely separate spell that does exactly the same thing as crucible, in the same arcanum, at the same level just for changing allotropes and conform to your real world understanding of chemistry, be my guest.<br /> <br /> I just think it's cmpletely pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T12:53:43-07:00","id":1458395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458389#post1458389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanna have a completely separate spell that does exactly the same thing as crucible, in the same arcanum, at the same level just for changing allotropes and conform to your real world understanding of chemistry, be my guest.<br /> <br /> I just think it's cmpletely pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's completely pointless only for you because you're the only one (out of the four recent posters in this thread) who thinks your solution to this problem works. For the rest of us, doing some extra work isn't pointless if it leads to a solution that we think actually works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Out of curiosity: Would you agree or disagree with the idea that Crucible could turn liquid water into ice because ice is more valuable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T15:49:40-07:00","id":1458421,"title":"","content":"If the point of the spell is making it more valuable or useful as a tool, yes. But that seems a very niche case and State Change offers a better solution for most practical situations.<br /> <br /> If my solution doesn't work, then I'd like to know which one does. What would the required spell accomplish that Crucible doesn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","user":"EW-Matias","date":".  Typos 09-02-2021, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T20:16:20-07:00","id":1458444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458421#post1458421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the point of the spell is making it more valuable or useful as a tool, yes. But that seems a very niche case and State Change offers a better solution for most practical situations.<br /> <br /> If my solution doesn't work, then I'd like to know which one does. What would the required spell accomplish that Crucible doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just coming in without knowledge of the past discussions:<br /> <br /> A spell that doesn\u2019t target an object/tool, but molecules. A Matter spell for sure. Likely still Weaving, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T00:05:59-07:00","id":1458473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458421#post1458421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the point of the spell is making it more valuable or useful as a tool, yes. But that seems a very niche case and State Change offers a better solution for most practical situations.<br /> <br /> If my solution doesn't work, then I'd like to know which one does. What would the required spell accomplish that Crucible doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since OP asks about allotropes, and not only coal to diamonds, I'd design a spell which specifically turns a material into a different allotrope. Even with your intepretation of Crucible, it can only do so from a less valuable allotrope to a more valueable allotrope. You could design a Fraying version of Crucible to make the reverse possible (thus also creating a second spell for this purpose), but you're still constrained by the spell changing value and only within certain limits. You would not be able to turn a material into an allotrope which does not have a different value (as represented by Availability) as that would definitely be outside the scope of Crucible. You're also constrained in how much Availability may change. It may at most triple in value, provided you spend a Reach on it.<br /> <br /> The spell I'd design would be able to turn a whole lump of coal (provided it's already pure enough; zCrucible could actually help with that step) into a diamond of equivalent mass, which Crucible can't do because Crucible (with the Reach option) can at most turn a lump of coal into a diamond with an Availability rating of 3. Such a diamond would be tiny and/or relatively impure.<br /> <br /> I would personally argue that a single lump of coal likely has no Availability at all. Rather, a sack of coal for a household coal grill would have a collective Availability of 1, which would definitely be impossible to transform into diamonds that would have anything close to the original object's size without exceeding the Availability limits of Crucible. And transforming a whole sack of coal into a single, small diamond would definitely be outside the scope of Crucible as nothing in the spell even remotely suggests you could compensate by removing a majority of the subject's mass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T07:50:53-07:00","id":1458513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458444#post1458444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just coming in without knowledge of the past discussions:<br /> <br /> A spell that doesn\u2019t target an object/tool, but molecules. A Matter spell for sure. Likely still Weaving, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) why target molecules? This about a lump o coal and diamond.<br /> 2) Ok, you make a new spell that targets molecules... what does it do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T08:05:24-07:00","id":1458518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458473#post1458473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since OP asks about allotropes, and not only coal to diamonds, I'd design a spell which specifically turns a material into a different allotrope. Even with your intepretation of Crucible, it can only do so from a less valuable allotrope to a more valueable allotrope. You could design a Fraying version of Crucible to make the reverse possible (thus also creating a second spell for this purpose), but you're still constrained by the spell changing value and only within certain limits. You would not be able to turn a material into an allotrope which does not have a different value (as represented by Availability) as that would definitely be outside the scope of Crucible. You're also constrained in how much Availability may change. It may at most triple in value, provided you spend a Reach on it.<br /> <br /> The spell I'd design would be able to turn a whole lump of coal (provided it's already pure enough; zCrucible could actually help with that step) into a diamond of equivalent mass, which Crucible can't do because Crucible (with the Reach option) can at most turn a lump of coal into a diamond with an Availability rating of 3. Such a diamond would be tiny and/or relatively impure.<br /> <br /> I would personally argue that a single lump of coal likely has no Availability at all. Rather, a sack of coal for a household coal grill would have a collective Availability of 1, which would definitely be impossible to transform into diamonds that would have anything close to the original object's size without exceeding the Availability limits of Crucible. And transforming a whole sack of coal into a single, small diamond would definitely be outside the scope of Crucible as nothing in the spell even remotely suggests you could compensate by removing a majority of the subject's mass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that OP's examples all imply improvment, even if what is better is contextual (betrer for some intened purpose), and thus Crucible shoul work. If you want to make sonetjing worse, yesh you might need another spell but I do not think you need anew one. There propably aleeady is some spell that does exactly what you want... Well, I guess there isn't an inverse Crucible, but I think that's an easy inversion like Nigredo/Albedo situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T08:05:34-07:00","id":1458519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458513#post1458513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) why target molecules? This about a lump o coal and diamond.<br /> 2) Ok, you make a new spell that targets molecules... what does it do?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Because things like that IMO often matter for Supernal spells. A lump of coal is a lump of coal, not a specifically aligned mass of carbon. You know, Symbols and universals and categories and all that. <br /> <br /> 2) What you\u2019ve wanted to starting from your first suggestion in this line of discussion, I\u2019d wager. <br /> <br /> Of course, I\u2019m rather lenient on things like this, so always take it with a grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T08:40:24-07:00","id":1458525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458518#post1458518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that OP's examples all imply improvment, even if what is better is contextual (betrer for some intened purpose), and thus Crucible shoul work. If you want to make sonetjing worse, yesh you might need another spell but I do not think you need anew one. There propably aleeady is some spell that does exactly what you want... Well, I guess there isn't an inverse Crucible, but I think that's an easy inversion like Nigredo/Albedo situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Would Ruling be enough, or would Weaving be required to change an element from one allotrope to another?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is the core question clearly stated in the opening post, and the question that has been discussed over six pages in this thread.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I still don't think Crucible would work because the singular effect of Crucible is to improve the value of the subject (either value as a tool, or financial value). Transforming it from one substance to another is, in my opinion, clearly beyond the scope of the spell. One of the examples is making a diamond purer and more beautiful.<br /> Rereading the spell, I also notice that it's worded to only bestow the Availability increase to items that are already valuable. If we simplify the spell to its fundamentals, I'd say that Crucible makes an object better for its intended purpose. A tool gains 8-Again, and a valuable object gains more value. A lump of coal is neither, because it's a type of fuel. If we extrapolate the core effect of Crucible to cover fuel as a category, it's going to make it more energy rich and thus burn stronger and/or for longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T09:45:34-07:00","id":1458535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458383#post1458383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Coal and diamond are both 100% carbon</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll cop to having apparently misunderstood the molecular diagram I saw of coal before, but I'm still finding a definition of coal that refers to it as &quot;a mixture of high-molecular-weight polycyclic aromatic compounds, such as benzene (C6H6), toluene (C6H5CH3), xylene (C6H4(CH3)2), naphthalene (C10H8), anthracene (C14H10), pyrene (C16H10) and their derivatives, with high mass fraction of carbon, as well as of water and volatile substances&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not an accurate comparison to water, but still not 100% carbon the way a pure diamond would be.<br /> <br /> A better comparison would be to wine, and whether it makes sense for a purification spell to approach that substance in terms of being impure water rather than a substance in its own right. I think for the sake of consistency and relieving Storytellers of the burden of needing to litigate a bunch of cases that try to extend something far beyond its likely intentions, it's best to go with the idea that such a thing qualifies primarily as however somebody would interact with it.<br /> <br /> Other spells there may be, but specifying effect matters for the sake of things like rotes and praxes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[citation needed]</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the description in Transubstantiation might be the closest thing to a singular citation, and Alter Integrity and Shrink/Grow are next along, but it's really mostly a thing acquired from a holistic reading of the magic, how it's understood and applied, as well as gathered from how writers talk about the thing across years.<br /> <br /> Like, speaking of the Grow spell, there's magic under the same dot level as Crucible that will make that lump of coal the size of an adult human, on the basis of a spell imago to make the Supernal symbol of it move closer to reality. Presumably the end result entails the thing consisting of extra molecules that come out of nowhere (although maybe not, maybe a Sleeper examining the thing with an electron tunnelling microscope would find that it Dissonantly consists of fewer molecules than something of its size should be and they're arrayed in a manner impossible to conceive), but that's not a detail that the mage needs to account for at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>can be</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any instance in any book other than the Chronicler's Guide that treats magic as though it is not?<br /> <br /> For the idea that it's not just that the books have as yet not depicted any spells or mages who engage with subjects in terms of directly targeting and manipulating in terms of molecular composition (despite ample opportunity to introduce such things with at least the Free Council) but that it's specifically not how magic can work, my own reasons include that it relieves a lot of headaches for trying to reconcile the effects of spells with a deeper understanding of chemistry and physics (we don't need to act as though tactile telekinesis is the reason Superman can lift buildings without them collapsing under their own weight), and because I find the standard for how imagos and the Supernal work to make magic more understandable and approachable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 09-03-2021, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T11:09:02-07:00","id":1458544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458535#post1458535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll cop to having apparently misunderstood the molecular diagram I saw of coal before, but I'm still finding a definition of coal that refers to it as &quot;a mixture of high-molecular-weight polycyclic aromatic compounds, such as benzene (C6H6), toluene (C6H5CH3), xylene (C6H4(CH3)2), naphthalene (C10H8), anthracene (C14H10), pyrene (C16H10) and their derivatives, with high mass fraction of carbon, as well as of water and volatile substances&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not an accurate comparison to water, but still not 100% carbon the way a pure diamond would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coal is overwhelmingly carbon with impurities. Diamonds can have impurities, too, it's what gives you diamonds of different colors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A better comparison would be to wine, and whether it makes sense for a purification spell to approach that substance in terms of being impure water rather than a substance in its own right. I think for the sake of consistency and relieving Storytellers of the burden of needing to litigate a bunch of cases that try to extend something far beyond its likely intentions, it's best to go with the idea that such a thing qualifies primarily as however somebody would interact with it. </div> </div> </div>Treat it as both. Wine is simultaneously its own thing, water with other stuff in it, and a poison; it can be interacted with on any of those levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well the description in Transubstantiation might be the closest thing to a singular citation, and Alter Integrity and Shrink/Grow are next along, but it's really mostly a thing acquired from a holistic reading of the magic, how it's understood and applied, as well as gathered from how writers talk about the thing across years. </div> </div> </div><i>Transubstantiation </i>lets you treat wine as a singular thing, it doesn't say you <i>have</i> to. For that particular spell there's probably not a reason not to treat wine as a singular substance, but the reach option exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, speaking of the Grow spell, there's magic under the same dot level as Crucible that will make that lump of coal the size of an adult human, on the basis of a spell imago to make the Supernal symbol of it move closer to reality. Presumably the end result entails the thing consisting of extra molecules that come out of nowhere (although maybe not, maybe a Sleeper examining the thing with an electron tunnelling microscope would find that it Dissonantly consists of fewer molecules than something of its size should be and they're arrayed in a manner impossible to conceive), but that's not a detail that the mage needs to account for at all. </div> </div> </div>This seems to be indicative of a common misunderstanding:<br /> <br /> Saying that you can exploit e.g. coal and diamonds being allotropes of carbon <i>is not the same thing</i> as saying that magic cannot just be magic, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any instance in any book other than the Chronicler's Guide that treats magic as though it is not? </div> </div> </div><i>Transmission </i>is one example. In the pre-errata draft of the book WiFi, Bluetooth, and &quot;radio waves&quot; were treated as separate things that could not be turned into each other with a Ruling spell (the spell specifically said that frequency couldn't be altered). It changed in the final release because that just doesn't make sense (wifi and bluetooth are radio, and if you can't change frequency you can't manipulate FM).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the idea that it's not just that the books have as yet not depicted any spells or mages who engage with subjects in terms of directly targeting and manipulating in terms of molecular composition (despite ample opportunity to introduce such things with at least the Free Council) but that it's specifically not how magic can work, my own reasons include that it relieves a lot of headaches for trying to reconcile the effects of spells with a deeper understanding of chemistry and physics (we don't need to act as though tactile telekinesis is the reason Superman can lift buildings without them collapsing under their own weight), and because I find the standard for how imagos and the Supernal work to make magic more understandable and approachable. </div> </div> </div>The writers aren't scientists, and they write what they know: which is fluffy. When they do try to write science-y it tends to be... not great and mostly pop-fluff (this isn't a dig, they're not scientists).<br /> <br /> And the science flavor <i>is </i>referenced heavily in the Free Council descriptions for paths and such.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T11:55:36-07:00","id":1458551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458525#post1458525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Would Ruling be enough, or would Weaving be required to change an element from one allotrope to another?&quot;<br /> <br /> This is the core question clearly stated in the opening post, and the question that has been discussed over six pages in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are dancing around the only important question: What do you want the spell to *actually do*. You change the allotrope, great, what does that mean? I think that my assumption that what you want is to make it more valuable is fair. So, you don't have to reinvent the wheel,, there's a spell for that already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458525#post1458525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, I still don't think Crucible would work because the singular effect of Crucible is to improve the value of the subject (either value as a tool, or financial value). Transforming it from one substance to another is, in my opinion, clearly beyond the scope of the spell. One of the examples is making a diamond purer and more beautiful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that''s the thing. I don't think any reasonable interpretation of the word &quot;substance&quot; can classify coal and diamonds as different substances. It's the ur-example of purification. In Spanish we literally call coals &quot;carb\u00f3n&quot;,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458525#post1458525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereading the spell, I also notice that it's worded to only bestow the Availability increase to items that are already valuable. If we simplify the spell to its fundamentals, I'd say that Crucible makes an object better for its intended purpose. A tool gains 8-Again, and a valuable object gains more value. A lump of coal is neither, because it's a type of fuel. If we extrapolate the core effect of Crucible to cover fuel as a category, it's going to make it more energy rich and thus burn stronger and/or for longer.`</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a fair reading, but I do think that it's the Mage the one who determines what the intended purpose is. And I think now we are getting into rules-lawering. I think the core idea of the spell is purification, making something into a purer and better version of itself with two specific mechanical effects to represent it. I think that aligns perfectly with the uses the OP implied.<br /> <br /> I'll make it more explicit: my first post came from the assumption you want to make the coal more valuable. If that's correct, my suggestion is to use Crucible. If you want to do the inverse, I guess it makes sense to create an Anti-crucible (although many Matter spells list variable Practices, although it's debatable if that is intended or just a space saving measure). If what you want to do with the diamond or graphite is not related to beauty, value, or tool-use, perhaps you just want to make it harder, then use Alter Integrity or State Change. In the end, neither the game systems nor the in-game metaphysics care for scientific concepts like allotropes, just with what you are *actually* trying to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T15:14:05-07:00","id":1458574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458551#post1458551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that''s the thing. <b> I don't think any reasonable interpretation of the word &amp;quot;substance&amp;quot; can classify coal and diamonds as different substances. </b> It's the ur-example of purification. In Spanish we literally call coals &amp;quot;carb\u00f3n&amp;quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Supernal interpretation ought to IMO. It runs on mysticism and symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:05:58-07:00","id":1458592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458574#post1458574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Supernal interpretation ought to IMO. It runs on mysticism and symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I said, symbolically and mystically, coal becoming diamonds is the ultimate symbol of Purification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:33:56-07:00","id":1458598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458544#post1458544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Transubstantiation </i>lets you treat wine as a singular thing, it doesn't say you <i>have</i> to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though that's not reading very deeply into the statement &quot;The Stygian Mysteries teach that purity is a perceptual concept&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Transmission </i>is one example. In the pre-errata draft of the book WiFi, Bluetooth, and &quot;radio waves&quot; were treated as separate things that could not be turned into each other with a Ruling spell (the spell specifically said that frequency couldn't be altered). It changed in the final release because that just doesn't make sense (wifi and bluetooth are radio, and if you can't change frequency you can't manipulate FM).</div> </div> </div> </div>But does the spell let you shorten the wavelength into microwaves, into gamma rays? If they're all one form of radio, then changing the wavelength while being confined to the form of radio is more akin to altering the shape of coal then turning it into an alternative form of diamond. I would look at the finalised form as designating electromagnetic radiation that transmits communication as the Form; inclusive of WiFi and Bluetooth, but exclusive of things with greater or lesser frequency, even when the spell includes modifications to wavelength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writers aren't scientists</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I get what you mean, but I still think this is the kind of broad statement that one should be cautious with; Dave Brookshaw has actually worked in archaeology, and indeed applied much of that technical knowledge to one of his chronicles (and probably makes significant contributions to things like his work on Mummy and The Sundered World). <br /> <br /> Still, I think this doesn't really work as an argument in a case where the subject in question can comfortably be not scientific. This isn't a case of somebody misrepresenting something with bad technobabble, it's describing a way of harnessing reality that explicitly runs on philosophical concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the science flavor <i>is </i>referenced heavily in the Free Council descriptions for paths and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is. It's not mentioned at all in the descriptions of Acanthus, Mastigos and Thyrsus, and for Moros and Obrimos, one mentions modern materials but without terms that specifically suggest Matter magic would be applied in their initial development, and the other describes scientific inquiry as a form of pattern recognition for the Path to use equal to theology, and describes mechanics and electrical engineering as a form of techn\u00e9, the ability to use scientific activity as a yantra. Thus, a symbolic reference to aid in imago forming. It has the same standing as a character's capacity to use a Shadow Name based on the persona of being a scientist insofar as it's the literal form the imago takes. <br /> <br /> In either case, I think the references are light, and need to be placed in the proper context. I find that the Free Council relationship with science is less about asserting new ways for spells to target things and more on promoting science as a way for people that are not mages to harness the world and arguing that the results have a wonder at least equal to what spells can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:54:19-07:00","id":1458601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458592#post1458592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as I said, symbolically and mystically, coal becoming diamonds is the ultimate symbol of Purification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I don\u2019t think (alchemical) purification in this context necessarily implies using the Practice of Perfecting. After all, turning lead into gold is a similar thing, but that\u2019s done by Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T22:51:16-07:00","id":1458620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458598#post1458598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though that's not reading very deeply into the statement &quot;The Stygian Mysteries teach that purity is a perceptual concept&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Perceptual i.e. malleable based on viewpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But does the spell let you shorten the wavelength into microwaves, into gamma rays? </div> </div> </div>Gamma radiation is defined as &quot;radiation from nuclear decay&quot;, so you couldn't get gamma but you could get X-ray (same freq range).<br /> <br /> Some radio waves (such as wifi) are already microwaves, so yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 09-04-2021, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T11:29:17-07:00","id":1458696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458601#post1458601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps, but I don\u2019t think (alchemical) purification in this context necessarily implies using the Practice of Perfecting. After all, turning lead into gold is a similar thing, but that\u2019s done by Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>But lead and gold *sctually are* different substances, for any difinition of substance. Whereas coal and diamonds are the same substance, carbon. One is just purer and a different molecular structure.<br /> <br /> Is like saying hollow bricks and solid bricks are a different substance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T11:41:58-07:00","id":1458699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458598#post1458598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> find that the Free Council relationship with science is less about asserting new ways for spells to target things and more on promoting science as a way for people that are not mages to harness the world and arguing that the results have a wonder at least equal to what spells can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are taking a very hard stance on something that is presented as a in game controversy. It's the central foundation of the Free Council that Humans can ideed change the Supernal through their collective practice of Science, Art and Culture. Science isn't *merely* a meaphor fir some Supernal Truth, Science can and does create new Supernal Truths. And whether that's strictly right or not is up for in game debate, but the setting info does tell us the Free Council has innovated new ways to use Magic, and is constantly looking for more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T14:29:13-07:00","id":1458729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458696#post1458696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But lead and gold *sctually are* different substances, for any difinition of substance. Whereas coal and diamonds are the same substance, carbon. One is just purer and a different molecular structure.<br /> <br /> Is like saying hollow bricks and solid bricks are a different substance.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I say that Coal and Diamond are different things too for mystical, Supernal purposes\u2026 but similar enough in their Fallen forms that, instead of the usual Patterning that would be required, you only need Weaving to bridge the gap between them. Science being applied to magic to make magic easier.<br /> Apply even more science to know what molecules are, and you can go \u201cOf course Coal and Diamond are separate. This? Oh, this is just me Perfecting molecular bonds. And whaddaya know, I got diamond out of coal. Convenient, yes?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 09-04-2021, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T20:26:50-07:00","id":1458766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458729#post1458729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I say that Coal and Diamond are different things too for mystical, Supernal purposes\u2026 but similar enough in their Fallen forms that, instead of the usual Patterning that would be required, you only need Weaving to bridge the gap between them. Science being applied to magic to make magic easier.<br /> Apply even more science to know what molecules are, and you can go \u201cOf course Coal and Diamond are separate. This? Oh, this is just me Perfecting molecular bonds. And whaddaya know, I got diamond out of coal. Convenient, yes?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems unmoored from sense and reason. The books don't say anything even close to any of that. All of us can play however we want, but those are not the rules nor the setting as they are presented in the game. If the designers thought any of that, they failef to write it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T22:14:34-07:00","id":1458780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458696#post1458696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But lead and gold *sctually are* different substances, for any difinition of substance. Whereas coal and diamonds are the same substance, carbon. One is just purer and a different molecular structure.<br /> <br /> Is like saying hollow bricks and solid bricks are a different substance.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are composed of the same chemical <i>element</i>, but they are <i>by definition</i> different substances as they have different chemical compositions (in arrangement) and different qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-05-2021, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T01:19:19-07:00","id":1458791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458766#post1458766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems unmoored from sense and reason. The books don't say anything even close to any of that. All of us can play however we want, but those are not the rules nor the setting as they are presented in the game. If the designers thought any of that, they failef to write it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting\u2019s magic ultimately runs on symbolism, not physics. The game\u2019s tagline is Modern Sorcery, not Sufficiently Advanced Technology. Quite moored as I see it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hey you know what\u2026 Maybe Crucible can do what you suggest; not by default but with a Reach option. Maybe +2 Reach. The very existence of this discussion means that there\u2019s enough ambiguity for the spell\u2019s effects, and Reach is how ambiguity is covered, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 09-05-2021, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T20:07:01-07:00","id":1458916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458780#post1458780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are composed of the same chemical <i>element</i>, but they are <i>by definition</i> different substances as they have different chemical compositions (in arrangement) and different qualities.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, ice is a different substance from water? Just making sure.<br /> <br /> Edit; I checked and I can't find any reference to Composition changing with molecular structure. All the definitions I find boil it down to it's formula.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","user":"EW-Matias","date":". 09-05-2021, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T02:39:36-07:00","id":1458975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1438336-how-to-coal-to-diamond?p=1458916#post1458916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, ice is a different substance from water? Just making sure.<br /> <br /> Edit; I checked and I can't find any reference to Composition changing with molecular structure. All the definitions I find boil it down to it's formula.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely first result on google (LibreTexts, a collection of univeristy material supported by several universities and the US Department of Education): &quot;Chemical composition refers to the <b>arrangement</b>, type, and ratio of atoms in molecules of chemical substances. Chemical composition varies when chemicals are added or subtracted from a substance, when the ratio of substances changes, or when other chemical changes occur in chemicals.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Me